WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.469
The conflict between Israel and Palestine
is one of the most complex and complicated

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:11.820
in international politics.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.183
And also, as you all know by now, one of the
most controversial situations we can find

00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:19.331
in the entire world. Well, in order to make
it easier, in this video, we will tackle one

00:00:19.331 --> 00:00:20.720
of the most delicate issues:

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.610
The Israeli settlements in the West Bank…

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.610
And this is a major issue with almost all
countries finding these settlements to be

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.290
a serious violation of international law.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.230
In the last 40 years, even all the administrations
in the United States has taken a position

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.580
against them. And when I say them, I mean
all of them.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.620
Yes, this matter has even compromised the
special relationship between the US and Israel.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.870
And I’m not just talking about governments
like Jimmy Carter´s, not at all.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:48.890
Indeed, Ronald Reagan himself demanded the
immediate freeze of any new settlements as

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.890
he claimed they were an evident obstacle to
peace. George H. W. Bush threatened to take

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.760
disciplinary measures of an economic nature.
Then Bill Clinton proposed a law to “punish”

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.010
Israel by reducing American assistance.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.100
Even today, Trump´s administration has asked
Israel to stop being such a “pain in the

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.220
ass” about it.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.720
“Since taking office in January, Trump has
publicly asked Netanyahu to constrain settlement

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.810
construction but has not condemned it. The
State Department has said that it is not helpful

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.939
to the peace process”. Jerusalem Post.
So what do you think Israel has done in the

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:22.170
face of all this criticism? Well, they have
basically ignored it all and have kept expanding

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.170
the settlements.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.950
But, ok, now we are here, you might be wondering:
What are these settlements and what do they

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:32.659
really mean? Well, let’s see…

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:35.859
(SETTLERS AND SETTLEMENTS)

00:01:35.859 --> 00:01:40.390
The first thing we need to know is that, according
to agreements that have been reached, the

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:44.840
territory or “state” of Palestine is formed
by what it is today known as the West Bank

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.100
and the Gaza Strip.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:50.240
These territories correspond to the political
map prior to the Six-Day War, after which

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:55.359
Israel occupied these territories, which used
to belong to Jordan. So, the settlements are

00:01:55.359 --> 00:01:59.429
essentially communities… villages, towns
and cities, that Israel has been building

00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:04.590
since 1970 in the West Bank… Territory of
the future Palestinian state. And it is not

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.439
just a few houses we are talking about...

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:11.410
The West Bank is a small territory, at barely
5,600 sq. km. That’s about the size of the

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:12.630
state of Delaware.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:16.819
Even so, today (and this is not considering
East Jerusalem) there are 131 settlements...

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:23.010
And, furthermore, there are an additional
97 outposts. These are settlements as well,

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:28.130
but in these case, these settlements are illegal
even under Israeli law. These outposts were

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:30.579
built without the consent of the Israeli government.

00:02:30.579 --> 00:02:35.659
That means there are more than 228 Israeli
settlements around the West Bank. Many are

00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:40.060
in places of relevant value, like aquifers,
and that makes it more complicated because

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.590
roads and infrastructure need to be set up
in order to connect them.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.580
Besides, Israel needs to protect these settlements
and that involves police patrolling around

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:52.409
the West Bank, which affects the mobility
of Palestinians, and makes economic development

00:02:52.409 --> 00:02:54.450
more difficult.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:03:00.310
And the problem isn't just the existence of
these settlements, it’s that they don´t

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.319
stop growing:

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:05.361
In the last year, more than 2000 new buildings
have started to be constructed, and there

00:03:05.361 --> 00:03:08.909
are plans to build more than 30,000 in the
next coming years.

00:03:08.909 --> 00:03:13.189
Obviously, there are also schools, medical
centres, synagogues… and so on.

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:17.870
And what’s the result of all this? Well,
take a look at this chart to see how the population

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:25.090
has evolved:
So, now some of you might be thinking: well

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.700
what’s the problem?

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.379
Those who are pro-settlement claim these are
population centres are growing where there

00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:31.450
used to be nothing.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:35.180
Consider what the Mayor of Ma'ale Adumim says
about one of the main settlements.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.730
“We didn’t steal the land from anybody
[...] “It was built on empty hills. You

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:43.700
can see there — the desert, rocks and sand.
Now you have a living city.”Benny Kashriel,

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:48.180
Mayor of Ma'ale Adumim.
Ma'ale Adumim is a city of 40,000 inhabitants,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.849
with schools, kindergartens, a theatre, a
library, an industrial centre… according

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:54.129
to the residents there, it is a complete city.

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:55.769
Alright, so again, what’s the problem?

00:03:55.769 --> 00:04:00.670
The problem is that in order to solve the
Israel-Palestine conflict, all parties agree

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.819
that two states are necessary: One being Israel,
and two being Palestine.

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:08.900
But with all the settlements… Palestinian
sovereignty in the West Bank will be in serious

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.379
danger, because Israel has already said they
will never give up sovereignty over these

00:04:12.379 --> 00:04:16.870
places. And that includes the roads, the infrastructure,
the security controls...

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:20.900
Let´s be clear: Palestinian will be unable
to become an effective and autonomous state

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:25.210
with such limitations, especially considering
these settlements won't stop growing.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:29.220
“Settlements are illegal under international
law and present one of the main impediments

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:33.540
to peace”. Nickolay Mladenov, United Nations
envoy on Middle East peace.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:38.930
So, now we can understand why this topic makes
everybody so tense…

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:43.490
(MORE AND MORE TENSION)

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:48.970
The tension over Netanyahu's settlement policy
hasn't stopped growing since 2015.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:53.451
The situation has reached a point that, on
the 23th of December 2016, the UN Security

00:04:53.451 --> 00:04:58.970
Council passed resolution 2334 that strongly
condemns the Israeli settlement policy.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:03.670
“The Security Council reaffirms that the
establishment by Israel of settlements in

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:09.060
the Palestinian territory occupied since 1967,
including East Jerusalem, has no legal validity

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:13.290
and constitutes a flagrant violation under
international law and a major obstacle to

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:18.250
the achievement of the two-State solution
and a just, lasting and comprehensive peace”.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.640
Resolution 2334 of Security Council (United
Nations)

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:24.450
This resolution could be passed because, for
the first time, the US didn't use their right

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.950
to veto the resolution. And, well, this is
something that made Netanyahu's government

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.110
really furious.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:32.380
The Prime Minister didn't hesitate in describing
the situation as absurd;

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:37.250
He even accused Barack Obama’s administration
in public of trying to carry out a “shameful

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.450
anti-Israeli manoeuvre”.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.720
So yeah, he was pretty angry.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.670
But these resolution shouldn't have taken
Netanyahu by surprise given some of the decisions

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:48.330
he announced in 2016 and confirmed in 2017.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:55.050
On the other hand, the Israeli government
has started a new settlement in the West Bank,

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.470
the first in two decades.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:06:00.980
So, Israel has not only decided to encourage
the existing settlements… but they’ve

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.240
even started a new one.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.220
On the other hand (and maybe empowered by
the alleged good relations with Trump) the

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:10.450
parliament in Israel, after lots of controversy,
finally passed a new law at the beginning

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:16.960
of 2017. This law legalizes around 4,000 houses
built on Palestinian private property; houses

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:21.080
that the Israeli Supreme Court had even ordered
to be dismantled...

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.410
“The rules of the game have changed with
Donald Trump’s arrival as president. We

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:28.420
no longer have our hands tied as in the time
of Barack Obama. Now we can finally build”.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:29.420
Meir Turgeman, Jerusalem Deputy Mayor

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.740
Hey, as we said before, the fact Trump might
look closer to Israel doesn´t mean that his

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.180
administration isn't also tired of this settlement
issue...

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:39.970
That is why, in order to try to regain Trump´s
favor, Jerusalem has committed to starting

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:45.590
a new policy that seems to slow down the growth
of existing settlements and forbid outposts

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.320
completely...
But the new policy is so cryptic and complicated

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:51.160
that it seems very likely the settlements
will keep growing.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.270
And now you probably have another question:
Why do these settlements grow so much?

00:06:55.270 --> 00:07:02.880
Well, pay close attention...
(THE INEXPLICABLE POLICY)

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:08.550
Think about it: Why do so many Israelis want
to live in these conflict zones?

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:12.710
Is it maybe because there are some valuable
natural resources to be exploited? Well, not

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.810
really. The explanation is… much less creative.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:19.750
The government of Israel is subsidizing the
establishment of these settlements...

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:25.220
That´s right, the government in Israel co-finances
the construction of houses, creating discounts

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:29.900
of almost 70% for the price of land and offers
a great deal of financial aid.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:33.840
And you know what the result is? Houses are
an average of 40% cheaper than in the formal

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.000
territory of Israel.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.810
And that´s not all, the government of Israel
also ensures security and provides all kinds

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:45.080
of public services. So, as you can imagine,
the youth and many families see in these places

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:48.330
the possibility of having a better life than
the one they could have in Israel’s formal

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:49.330
territory.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:52.200
So how does Israel benefit from this?

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:56.330
Well… the truth is that they really don’t,
and in exchange they just get a bunch of political

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.920
and economic problems.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:01.610
These settlements aren´t just an obstacle
for the peace process and foreign policy,

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:03.950
they are also a big waste of public money.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:08.140
Look, with subsidies, security, expensive
public services... The Peace Now foundation

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:12.110
and the Adva Centre (both Israeli by the way)
estimate that the cost of these is more than

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:13.800
a billion dollars a year.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.480
In other words, this is nothing but an expensive,
nationalist policy, both for the citizens

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:24.420
of Palestine as well as those of Israel.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:30.280
DON´T GET FOOLED

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:34.270
But let me be absolutely clear, Israel is
country full of positive things.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:38.459
Unlike their neighbouring countries, Israel
is a consolidated democracy with strong civil

00:08:38.459 --> 00:08:41.419
liberties and a prosperous and innovative
economy.

00:08:41.419 --> 00:08:45.340
Many of the products and services we use everyday
wouldn't exist if it weren't for the technology

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:46.340
developed in Israel.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:50.630
And don't be fooled, putting an end to these
settlements wouldn´t mean an end to the conflict.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:51.840
Because there is a precedent:

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:56.800
In 2005, Israel left the Gaza Strip completely,
stopping all the settlements and removing

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.100
all civilians and soldiers.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:03.320
And the result was neither peace nor prosperity.
The Strip is now controlled by Hamas radicals,

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:07.550
and it is even in conflict with the government
of Palestine itself and the situation isn't

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.370
good from a humanitarian perspective…

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:13.890
But it definitely doesn't justify the settlement
policy of Israel and their lack of commitment

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:14.890
towards a peace agreement.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:20.020
Now, the question is: Is there any possible
solution to this conflict? Well, more and

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:23.780
more experts claim the solution needs to be
a bottom-up strategy:

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:27.780
That is to say: encourage economic development
in the West Bank, establish a dialogue and

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:32.100
understanding where trade relations between
Israelis and Palestinians are normal, and

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.080
let the National Authorities in Palestine
have more jurisdiction.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.320
These all requires time, but more than that,
it needs COMMITMENT.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:44.080
So, now it is your turn: what do you think
should happen with the settlements? Leave

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.210
your answer on the comments as well as the
survey.

